- action(n1, "start"): Hallucinates an initial step; the source description begins directly with `"HelloWorld.HelloWorld"`, not a separate start action.
- action(n3, "End"): Hallucinates a final action step; the source only states the process `"comes to an end"` immediately after `"HelloWorld.HelloWorld"`, without an intermediate task.
- precedence(i1, n1), precedence(n1, n2), precedence(n2, n3), precedence(n3, e1): Introduces extraneous control-flow edges that violate the exact chronology described as `"HelloWorld.HelloWorld, and then the process comes to an end."`